      "text": "To determine the new class mean after all 36 students have taken the test, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of the 30 students who took the test the first time.\n2. Calculate the total score of the 6 students who took the test the second time.\n3. Find the combined total score for all 36 students.\n4. Determine the new class mean by dividing the combined total score by the total number of students.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total score of the 30 students.**\n\nThe mean score of the 30 students is 72%. Therefore, the total score for these 30 students is:\n\\[\n30 \\times 72 = 2160\n\\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total score of the 6 students.**\n\nThe mean score of the 6 students is 78%. Therefore, the total score for these 6 students is:\n\\[\n6 \\times 78 = 468\n\\]\n\n**Step 3: Find the combined total score for all 36 students.**\n\nAdd the total scores from the two groups of students:\n\\[\n2160 + 468 = 2628\n\\]\n\n**Step 4: Determine the new class mean.**\n\nThe new class mean is the combined total score divided by the total number of students:\n\\[\n\\frac{2628}{36} = 73\n\\]\n\nThus, the new class mean is \\(\\boxed{73}\\).",
